---
title: "11 · Delivery after signing"
description: How the services of a signed contract open their cases, how to follow their delivery, and how to end a service.
sidebar:
  order: 12
  label: "11 · Delivery after signing"
---

**Who:** the person in charge and the departments that deliver the services. **Where:** the opportunity › **Services** tab, **Delivery** column; or the client's **Services** tab.

## When the cases open

A signed contract starts its delivery when it receives its first payment: once a payment is recorded on an invoice of the contract, Operon opens the first cases.

| Service type | What opens |
|---|---|
| **One-off** | One case of the service's default case type. |
| **Recurring** | One case for each cycle, a set number of days before the cycle's work due date. |
| **Continuous** | No case. The service is only invoiced on its billing calendar. |

A case of a service with prerequisites stays with the opportunity owner, with its prerequisite checklist on top, until every item is done; then it goes to the department manager. The service type, the case type and the prerequisites are set on the service's **Delivery** card (see [2 · Services & Packages](/en/crm/services-packages/)).

## Follow the delivery

The **Delivery** column reads:

- **Not started**: signed, no case linked yet and not onboarded (waiting for the first payment);
- **Started**: a case is linked, or the contract is onboarded and has a continuous service;
- **Completed**: every service is one-off and every case is completed;
- **Ended**: the service has been ended.

Select the value to open the service's delivery: its status, the next work due date, when the next case opens, the next invoice, its **Cases** and its **Billing history**. If a case cannot open automatically, the drawer says why under **Cannot open automatically** and links to where it is fixed.

{% screenshot id="crm/delivery-drawer" caption="The delivery of a signed one-off service that has not started yet." /%}

On the contract list, the **Delivery** value of a contract opens a read-only overview of all its services.

## Start a case by hand

Before the first payment, or for a cycle whose case has not opened yet, select **Start case** in the service's delivery. The case is linked to the contract and carries the same prerequisite checklist. Only someone who can edit the opportunity, or a tenant admin, sees **Start case**.

## End a service

{% steps %}

1. Open the service's delivery and select **End service**.
2. Enter the **End date** and the **Reason**.
3. Select **End service**.

{% /steps %}

No new cases open for the service after the end date, and invoices due after the end date that are not issued yet are cancelled. Cases already opened are not changed. A service that is part of a package ends the whole package and every service in it.

{% screenshot id="crm/delivery-end-service" caption="Ending a service: the end date and the reason." /%}
